From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cq8725s-ayn-odin3: load the SoCCP firmware

The bootloader leaves an early SoCCP image running in D0 with no bus vote,
and once the APSS releases every system NoC vote for sleep the SoC never
comes back from SYSTEM_SUSPEND or s2idle. Point the SoCCP (9019/9020) at
the AYN firmware the image ships, so the driver reloads it, the SoCCP
parks in D3 and the boot bus vote is dropped. Without this the vote
stays: the Odin 3 wakes, but never reaches DDR low power.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
@@ -278,6 +278,10 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&remoteproc_soccp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8750/ayn/odin3/soccp.mbn";
+};
+
 &spk_amp_l {
 	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8750/ayn/odin3/aw883xx_acf.bin";
 };
